From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:26:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 053/342] bfs: growing a volume works

Growing a BFS volume (BFS_IOCTL_RESIZE, bfs_shell resizefs) failed in two
places:
* ResizeVisitor kept the allocator restricted to the range moved data
  had to go to, so MoveLog() could not get blocks for the larger log:
  "Failed to move the log area". The restriction is lifted once all data
  is out of the way.
* BlockAllocator::Reinitialize() called Initialize(true, true), which
  hands the allocator lock to _Initialize() to release it, without
  holding that lock: the unlock of a lock not held crashed. It now takes
  the lock first; Initialize() also releases it when it fails early.

Tested with bfs_shell on 300 MiB system volumes grown to 988 MiB and to
4060 MiB (checkfs clean before and after), and on the board: a grown
988 MiB system volume booting, a 540 MB file written and read back after a
power cycle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/BlockAllocator.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/ResizeVisitor.cpp  | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/BlockAllocator.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/BlockAllocator.cpp
index c9a28a1cda..39a5a61870 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/BlockAllocator.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/BlockAllocator.cpp
@@ -653,8 +653,11 @@ BlockAllocator::Initialize(bool full, bool alreadyLocked)
 	fNumBitmapBlocks = fVolume->NumBitmapBlocks();
 
 	fGroups = new(std::nothrow) AllocationGroup[fNumGroups];
-	if (fGroups == NULL)
+	if (fGroups == NULL) {
+		if (alreadyLocked)
+			recursive_lock_unlock(&fLock);
 		return B_NO_MEMORY;
+	}
 
 	if (!full)
 		return B_OK;
@@ -751,7 +754,11 @@ BlockAllocator::Reinitialize()
 		// starts a transaction before we get the allocator lock, as that
 		// would cause a deadlock
 
+	// Initialize() hands the lock over to _Initialize(), which releases it:
+	// it has to be ours first (no one else may use the groups meanwhile).
+	recursive_lock_lock(&fLock);
 	delete[] fGroups;
+	fGroups = NULL;
 	return Initialize(true, true);
 }
 
diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/ResizeVisitor.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/ResizeVisitor.cpp
index 353b7e50b6..25255f8114 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/ResizeVisitor.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/bfs/ResizeVisitor.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,11 @@ ResizeVisitor::Resize(off_t size, bool dryRun, disk_job_id job)
 	if (fDryRun)
 		return B_OK;
 
+	// The data is out of the way: the log may now take blocks outside the
+	// range moved data had to go to (growing, it extends into the area the
+	// larger block bitmap freed up).
+	GetVolume()->Allocator().SetAllowedRange(0, 0);
+
 	// move log and change file system size in the superblock
 	if (fShrinking) {
 		status = _ResizeVolume();
